Firefox on Haiku arm64: xptcall, NSPR/NSS in-tree, CPU-specific bits, headless mode

On top of HaikuPorts' firefox-157.0.1.patchset (x86_64 only, built there with clang) and
patches/spidermonkey:
- xptcall (xpcom/reflect/xptcall/md/unix/moz.build): the aarch64 stubs are plain AAPCS64 and
  OS-independent; build them for Haiku as for Linux and the BSDs.
- Navigator.platform and the UA's oscpu said "Haiku x86_64" on every CPU: name the build's CPU
  ("Haiku aarch64", as Linux says "Linux aarch64").
- nsSystemInfo.cpp: get_cpuid() (vendor, family, model, brand) exists on x86 only.
- No user-space CPU feature detection on Haiku arm64: ffvpx (config_unix_aarch64.h: neither
  getauxval() nor sched_getaffinity(), as the patchset does for x86_64), libvpx and libaom
  (aarch64_cpudetect.c) use the Armv8.0 baseline (Neon), as libvpx does on OpenBSD.
- NSPR, built in-tree (config/external/nspr): the Haiku branch of nsprpub/configure.in from
  HaikuPorts' nspr-4.39.patchset as moz.build defines, with the patchset's nsprpub changes
  (md/_haiku.{cfg,h}, prhaiku.cpp: the time zone from BTimeZone, ...) ported to the in-tree
  4.40 (reformatted upstream), md/_haiku.cfg extended to aarch64 (LP64, as x86_64), and
  prhaiku.cpp's libbe header kept at default visibility (in-tree code is built hidden).
- NSS, built in-tree by gyp: a "haiku" OS flavour (build/gyp_base.mozbuild, defines HAIKU and
  _DEFAULT_SOURCE in coreconf/config.gypi), the library part of HaikuPorts' nss-3.129.patchset,
  and <endian.h> for the karamel/libcrux headers on Haiku.
- nsBrowserApp.cpp: fontconfig's configuration ships in the application directory
  (fontconfig/fonts.conf); point FONTCONFIG_PATH there unless the environment sets it.
- nsAppRunner.cpp: allow headless mode (--headless, --screenshot) on Haiku: HeadlessWidget with
  the generic in-process compositor widget and the native nsLookAndFeel, as on macOS.

